{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRQXtqrymyZxciJggazM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019pqrmfsoA3wMHC3h4rLTVf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"find \"$TMPDIR\" | grep -c . ; du -sh \"$TMPDIR\"; \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft - <<'EOF'\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N16\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\",\"line\":32,\"summary\":\"The R3 test is flaky and breaks the unit gate: it requires the attempt name to be no longer than one random os.MkdirTemp name, but that suffix is a uint32 in decimal (1 to 10 digits), so shorter draws fail it. Measured 235 failures in 1000 runs; it also failed in a plain -run RunContinuity run. The comment at review_dispatch.go:2038 ('as long as the random suffix') carries the same wrong assumption. Compare against the longest random name (prefix plus 10 digits) instead of a sample.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N17\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\",\"line\":431,\"summary\":\"Carries R2-N8 and R3-N12: the claim lookup and the directory check are not atomic, so a resume or handoff that loses a race can get the directory refusal instead of pending. Established by reading.\",\"action\":\"Make the continuation claim and the runtime-directory check one step, or re-read the claim before refusing\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n{\"id\":\"N18\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":2053,\"summary\":\"Carries R3-N11: a run interrupted under an earlier engine used a random runtime directory; resuming it creates the stable path without telling the session, which still points at the removed checkout. The predecessor's safety.runtime_id is never compared. Transitional.\",\"action\":\"Refuse or warn on resume when the predecessor's safety.runtime_id differs from the attempt's path\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n{\"id\":\"N19\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":2092,\"summary\":\"Carries R3-N13: PlanReviewHandoff returns a refusal ending in 'then resume' although the operator asked for a handoff.\",\"action\":\"Word the remedy neutrally, such as 'then run again'\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n{\"id\":\"N20\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\",\"line\":42,\"summary\":\"Carries R3-N14: an os.Symlink error is fatal, so the test fails on Windows without the symlink privilege instead of skipping the link case.\",\"action\":\"Skip only the link case when os.Symlink is not permitted\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n{\"id\":\"N21\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\",\"line\":699,\"summary\":\"Carries R3-N15: a session continued into a new round belongs to a new attempt, so its checkout path differs from the one the session saw. Outside this spec's resume scope; established by reading.\",\"action\":\"Decide in a follow-up spec whether continued rounds need a stable path or a path notice\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"}\n],\n\"prior_findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"R2-N8\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"review_run_continuity.go:413-433 still reads the claim then checks the directory non-atomically; review_dispatch.go:2092 now says a run may be starting; spec follow-up recorded; carried as N17.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N11\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_dispatch.go:2053-2077 derives the path from the attempt id only; no comparison with the predecessor's safety.runtime_id; carried as N18.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N12\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"Same defect as R2-N8, carried as N17.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N13\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_dispatch.go:2092 still ends 'then resume' and delegation_handoff.go:347 returns it; carried as N19.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N14\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_run_runtime_dir_test.go:41-43 still calls t.Fatal on a Symlink error; carried as N20.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N15\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_rounds.go:699 continues the session while the dispatch prepares a new attempt (review_dispatch.go:716-722), hence a new path; carried as N21.\"}\n],\n\"sweep\":\"Spec R1-R3, D1, L1-L3; this spec's code, test and manual diff including both locales and scaffold copies; run lifecycle (claim, runtime directory creation, failure paths, cleanupReviewResources), resume, handoff, abandonment release and round continuation; path safety; focused tests, 1000 repeats of the exclusivity test, vet, planned pose tools and both validate forms.\",\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N16\",\"rationale\":\"The socket-bound cause is addressed, but the assumption that the random suffix is always 10 digits is false.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The exclusive claim precedes directory creation and os.Mkdir is exclusive; the race left affects only which refusal is returned (N17).\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"No record, brief or adapter command changes.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The attempt id is matched by a strict pattern; existing paths and links are refused.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Resume and handoff both consult the check; task runs do not use this function. Focused continuity and handoff tests passed locally with a private XDG_STATE_HOME.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Failures name the directory and the reason in the error or run record.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Earlier records keep their meaning; the transitional gap for resuming older runs is N18.\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N16\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-300d93d23f3c2998\",\"rationale\":\"The cause was a random path removed by cleanup; a per-attempt path recreates it (D1). The design assessment observed no structural delta, so no mapping is owed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Both manuals state the stable path, TMPDIR condition and remedy, matching the code; the pt-BR scaffold copy is identical and the English copy differs only by the contributor-mode block.\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Refusals name the path and a remedy; the wording gap is N19.\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"R1 and R2 are exercised by the resume test, R3 by the exclusivity and resume tests; the exclusivity test's flakiness is N16.\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The change stays in the runtime directory, its two continuation checks, tests and manuals.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Mode 0700, exclusive creation, no link following, cleanup identity checks unchanged; predictability falls within L2 and L3, which I found justified.\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"A stable name is smaller than changing the sealed brief to announce a new path; it would be invalid if one attempt could have two live runs.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the output tail shows warnings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-300d93d23f3c2998\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the gaps seen in the output tail are unobserved HTTP consumers, unrelated to this change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the scan reports itself incomplete for two older specs.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, 0 findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Sandbox rerun: 236 steps, 225 pass, 10 fail, 1 error. Some failures report sandbox ownership of /var/tmp or a file mode change; runtime socket, journey, capability and removal-ordering failures and the 600s timeout were not fully diagnosed; they are inferred environmental. The sealed evidence records a pass.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Sandbox rerun: 233 steps, 223 pass, 9 fail, 1 error, with the same kinds of failure; not all diagnosed. The sealed evidence records a pass.\"}\n]}\n```\nEOF","description":"Check the final draft against the rules"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2531,"cache_read_input_tokens":136377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2531},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"2007d423-aad8-45b4-9daa-6c1fe3c9ae9b","timestamp":"2026-11-26T10:47:43.595Z","request_id":"req_011ChRQXteDE26Q5wkHQd1in","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019pqrmfsoA3wMHC3h4rLTVf":{"command":"find \"$TMPDIR\" | grep -c . ; du -sh \"$TMPDIR\"; \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft - <<'EOF'\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N16\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\",\"line\":32,\"summary\":\"The R3 test is flaky and breaks the unit gate: it requires the attempt name to be no longer than one random os.MkdirTemp name, but that suffix is a uint32 in decimal (1 to 10 digits), so shorter draws fail it. Measured 235 failures in 1000 runs; it also failed in a plain -run RunContinuity run. The comment at review_dispatch.go:2038 ('as long as the random suffix') carries the same wrong assumption. Compare against the longest random name (prefix plus 10 digits) instead of a sample.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N17\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\",\"line\":431,\"summary\":\"Carries R2-N8 and R3-N12: the claim lookup and the directory check are not atomic, so a resume or handoff that loses a race can get the directory refusal instead of pending. Established by reading.\",\"action\":\"Make the continuation claim and the runtime-directory check one step, or re-read the claim before refusing\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n{\"id\":\"N18\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":2053,\"summary\":\"Carries R3-N11: a run interrupted under an earlier engine used a random runtime directory; resuming it creates the stable path without telling the session, which still points at the removed checkout. The predecessor's safety.runtime_id is never compared. Transitional.\",\"action\":\"Refuse or warn on resume when the predecessor's safety.runtime_id differs from the attempt's path\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n{\"id\":\"N19\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":2092,\"summary\":\"Carries R3-N13: PlanReviewHandoff returns a refusal ending in 'then resume' although the operator asked for a handoff.\",\"action\":\"Word the remedy neutrally, such as 'then run again'\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n{\"id\":\"N20\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\",\"line\":42,\"summary\":\"Carries R3-N14: an os.Symlink error is fatal, so the test fails on Windows without the symlink privilege instead of skipping the link case.\",\"action\":\"Skip only the link case when os.Symlink is not permitted\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n{\"id\":\"N21\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\",\"line\":699,\"summary\":\"Carries R3-N15: a session continued into a new round belongs to a new attempt, so its checkout path differs from the one the session saw. Outside this spec's resume scope; established by reading.\",\"action\":\"Decide in a follow-up spec whether continued rounds need a stable path or a path notice\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"}\n],\n\"prior_findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"R2-N8\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"review_run_continuity.go:413-433 still reads the claim then checks the directory non-atomically; review_dispatch.go:2092 now says a run may be starting; spec follow-up recorded; carried as N17.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N11\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_dispatch.go:2053-2077 derives the path from the attempt id only; no comparison with the predecessor's safety.runtime_id; carried as N18.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N12\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"Same defect as R2-N8, carried as N17.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N13\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_dispatch.go:2092 still ends 'then resume' and delegation_handoff.go:347 returns it; carried as N19.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N14\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_run_runtime_dir_test.go:41-43 still calls t.Fatal on a Symlink error; carried as N20.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N15\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_rounds.go:699 continues the session while the dispatch prepares a new attempt (review_dispatch.go:716-722), hence a new path; carried as N21.\"}\n],\n\"sweep\":\"Spec R1-R3, D1, L1-L3; this spec's code, test and manual diff including both locales and scaffold copies; run lifecycle (claim, runtime directory creation, failure paths, cleanupReviewResources), resume, handoff, abandonment release and round continuation; path safety; focused tests, 1000 repeats of the exclusivity test, vet, planned pose tools and both validate forms.\",\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N16\",\"rationale\":\"The socket-bound cause is addressed, but the assumption that the random suffix is always 10 digits is false.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The exclusive claim precedes directory creation and os.Mkdir is exclusive; the race left affects only which refusal is returned (N17).\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"No record, brief or adapter command changes.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The attempt id is matched by a strict pattern; existing paths and links are refused.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Resume and handoff both consult the check; task runs do not use this function. Focused continuity and handoff tests passed locally with a private XDG_STATE_HOME.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Failures name the directory and the reason in the error or run record.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Earlier records keep their meaning; the transitional gap for resuming older runs is N18.\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N16\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-300d93d23f3c2998\",\"rationale\":\"The cause was a random path removed by cleanup; a per-attempt path recreates it (D1). The design assessment observed no structural delta, so no mapping is owed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Both manuals state the stable path, TMPDIR condition and remedy, matching the code; the pt-BR scaffold copy is identical and the English copy differs only by the contributor-mode block.\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Refusals name the path and a remedy; the wording gap is N19.\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"R1 and R2 are exercised by the resume test, R3 by the exclusivity and resume tests; the exclusivity test's flakiness is N16.\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The change stays in the runtime directory, its two continuation checks, tests and manuals.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Mode 0700, exclusive creation, no link following, cleanup identity checks unchanged; predictability falls within L2 and L3, which I found justified.\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"A stable name is smaller than changing the sealed brief to announce a new path; it would be invalid if one attempt could have two live runs.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the output tail shows warnings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-300d93d23f3c2998\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the gaps seen in the output tail are unobserved HTTP consumers, unrelated to this change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the scan reports itself incomplete for two older specs.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, 0 findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Sandbox rerun: 236 steps, 225 pass, 10 fail, 1 error. Some failures report sandbox ownership of /var/tmp or a file mode change; runtime socket, journey, capability and removal-ordering failures and the 600s timeout were not fully diagnosed; they are inferred environmental. The sealed evidence records a pass.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Sandbox rerun: 233 steps, 223 pass, 9 fail, 1 error, with the same kinds of failure; not all diagnosed. The sealed evidence records a pass.\"}\n]}\n```\nEOF","description":"Check the final draft against the rules"}}}
