t use this function. Focused continuity and handoff tests passed locally with a private XDG_STATE_HOME.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Failures name the directory and the reason in the error or run record.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Earlier records keep their meaning; the transitional gap for resuming older runs is N18.\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N16\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-300d93d23f3c2998\",\"rationale\":\"The cause was a random path removed by cleanup; a per-attempt path recreates it (D1). The design assessment observed no structural delta, so no mapping is owed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Both manuals state the stable path, TMPDIR condition and remedy, matching the code; the pt-BR scaffold copy is identical and the English copy differs only by the contributor-mode block.\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Refusals name the path and a remedy; the wording gap is N19.\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"R1 and R2 are exercised by the resume test, R3 by the exclusivity and resume tests; the exclusivity test's flakiness is N16.\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The change stays in the runtime directory, its two continuation checks, tests and manuals.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"dis